@startuml dlq-inspection-recovery
title US-09: DLQ Inspection and Recovery - Bad Events Examined and Reprocessed

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Developer
queue "Kafka\nadsb.dlq / ais.dlq" as DLQ
participant "DLQ\nInspection Tool" as Tool
queue "Kafka\nadsb.raw / ais.raw" as Kafka
participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer

Developer -> Tool : consume from DLQ topic
Tool -> DLQ : read events
DLQ --> Tool : { raw_payload, rejection_reason, source_offset }

Developer -> Developer : inspect rejection reasons\nidentify root cause\n(e.g. schema change in feed)

alt event can be fixed and reprocessed
  Developer -> Tool : apply fix to raw payload
  Tool -> Kafka : republish corrected event\nto adsb.raw / ais.raw
  Kafka -> Consumer : consume corrected event
  Consumer -> Consumer : parse and process successfully

else event is genuinely bad data
  Developer -> Developer : discard - no further action needed\noriginal preserved in DLQ for audit
end

note over DLQ
  DLQ acts as an audit log of all
  bad events. Retention policy applies
  the same as any other Kafka topic.
end note

@enduml
